<programme start="20261108023000 +0000" stop="20261108060000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Hawaii at Texas-El Paso</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Rainbow Warriors (2-6, 1-4) visit the Miners (1-7, 0-4) for a Mountain West affair. The programs haven&apos;t met since 2004, when they were Western Athletic Conference foes. Hawaii traveled 4,255 miles to beat Northern Illinois 56-21 last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108060000 +0000" stop="20261108090000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">UCLA at Minnesota</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 8 UCLA Bruins (8-0) face the Minnesota Golden Gophers (5-3) at Huntington Bank Stadium for a Big Ten game. UCLA enters undefeated in eight games after shutting out Nevada 27-0, while Minnesota is coming off a 23-16 overtime defeat to Indiana.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261108090000 +0000" stop="20261108120000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Iowa at Northwestern</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 19 Hawkeyes seek their fifth straight victory over the Wildcats. Both sides are 6-2, 3-2 Big Ten. Iowa recorded its third shutout of the season, holding Wisconsin to nine first downs and 235 yards from scrimmage in a 30-0 decision last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
