<programme start="20261109030000 +0000" stop="20261109060000 +0000" channel="SEC ESPN Network"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Georgia at Ole Miss</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 10 Ole Miss Rebels (6-2) host the No. 2 Georgia Bulldogs (7-1) at Vaught-Hemingway Stadium for an SEC matchup. Georgia arrives after a 27-8 victory over Florida behind Nate Frazier, while Ole Miss beat Auburn 45-15, led by Trinidad Chambliss.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261109060000 +0000" stop="20261109090000 +0000" channel="SEC ESPN Network"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Oklahoma at Florida</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Oklahoma Sooners (4-4) visit No. 24 Florida Gators at Ben Hill Griffin Stadium for an SEC clash. Oklahoma fell 42-25 to South Carolina and relies on quarterback John Mateer, while Florida lost 27-8 to Georgia and looks to quarterback Aaron Philo.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
